AB  - This study explores the acceptance of digital health services among Emergency Medical Services (EMS) professionals in Northern Greece using the Technology Acceptance Model (TAM). Data from eighty-two (82) participants revealed a generally positive attitude towards digital transformation, emphasizing the need for further training in digital literacy. Key findings suggest that perceived usefulness (PU) and ease of use (PEOU) are critical drivers for the adoption of digital health technologies.
