AU  - Ohe K
PY  - 2026
T2  - Studies in health technology and informatics
VL  - 336
SP  - 1601-1602
AB  - Japan's national initiative for scientific infrastructure emphasizes equitable healthcare delivery in depopulated regions facing rapid aging and physician shortages. To address these challenges, we developed HeXEHRS, a cloud-based electronic health record (EHR) platform built on HL7 FHIR (R4) and aligned with JP Core profiles, serving as a reference implementation for Japanese clinics. HeXEHRS consists of a production-grade FHIR cloud server with native JP Core validation and terminology services and a standards-compliant client implemented with Svelte, supporting registration, documentation, ordering, and scheduling workflows. Integrated AI and digital-twin connectors enable summarization, speech recognition, and PHR integration. While prioritizing Japan's underserved areas, the architecture is applicable to clinics nationwide and offers a globally applicable approach to extend sustainable, interoperable healthcare services in remote or resource-limited regions worldwide.
